From 49c4d0f7e0a71f4662e779fbbe881b614515ffff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 00:00:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] NDNormalForm: a library sweep's eight inline re-proofs cite
 core and Mathlib; nf_update_last shared

A systematic exact?/apply? sweep of every have, obtain and private theorem
about core or Mathlib objects (gate 95, round 2 finding 1's kind):
- G1-G8 cite Nat.succ_mod_succ_eq_zero_iff, Nat.pos_of_mul_pos_left (2),
  Nat.div_lt_of_lt_mul, Nat.mul_div_cancel', List.ofFn_eq_nil_iff and
  List.ne_nil_of_length_pos (2) in place of their inline proofs;
- every rw [List.length_take, Nat.min_eq_left h] is List.length_take_of_le h;
- every foldl over l ++ [x] by foldl_append, foldl_cons, foldl_nil is
  List.foldl_concat.
nf_prefix_last and nf_sweep_record proved the same Function.update
completion of the parser's prefix array; it is now one private,
nf_update_last, cited by both. No statement changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PqpVTk5MM3PtshNwvNBXBw
